IoT Smart Energy Meter - Real-Time Power Monitoring, Billing & Energy Management - Using ESP32 + PZEM-004T + Blynk

2. Abstract
IoT Smart Energy Meter measures Voltage, Current, Power, Energy (kWh), Power Factor in real-time and sends data to mobile app. Users can see live usage, bill estimation, overload alerts, and control loads remotely. Replaces manual meter reading.

3. Introduction & Problem
Old meters - No real-time visibility, manual reading errors, no overload alert, high bills. Solution - Smart meter with live monitoring.

4. Objectives
Measure V, I, P, Energy accurately, Display on LCD + App, Calculate Units & Bill, Overload alert, Cloud storage, Remote ON/OFF.

5. Components
- ESP32 / NodeMCU ESP8266 - Main controller + WiFi
- PZEM-004T v3.0 + CT 100A - Measures V, I, P, Energy
- 16x2 LCD - Local display
- 4-Channel Relay - ON/OFF loads
- Buzzer, 5V SMPS, Wires
- Software: Arduino IDE, Blynk IoT, ThingSpeak
- Total Cost: Rs 1500 - 2500

6. Working
CT clips on live wire -> PZEM measures -> ESP32 calculates:
Energy = Power x Time / 1000 = kWh
Bill = Units x Rs 6.5
Data on LCD + Blynk every 10 sec. If Power > 2000W, Buzzer + App Alert.

Circuit:
PZEM TX -> ESP32 RX2 (GPIO 16), RX -> TX2 (GPIO 17)
LCD SDA -> 21, SCL -> 22, Relay -> 23, Buzzer -> 18

7. Code - Main Logic
float V = pzem.voltage();
float I = pzem.current();
float P = pzem.power();
float E = pzem.energy();
float bill = E * 6.5;
Blynk.virtualWrite(V0, V);
Blynk.virtualWrite(V1, I);
Blynk.virtualWrite(V2, P);
Blynk.virtualWrite(V3, E);
Blynk.virtualWrite(V4, bill);
8. Results
- 100W Bulb = 98W, 1000W Heater = 998W
- Accuracy 98-99%
- Saves 20-30% electricity
- Future: Prepaid, AI Bill Prediction, Solar

9. Conclusion
Provides real-time, accurate and user-friendly energy monitoring. Helps save electricity and reduce bills.

